cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Compressed Sensing using Generative Models
message: If you use this code, please cite both this repository and the original paper by Bora et al.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Renato
    family-names: Gallicola
  - given-names: Matteo
    family-names: Forlivesi
repository-code: https://github.com/RenatoGallicola/compressed-sensing-using-generative-models
abstract: >-
  Reproduction and extension of Bora et al. (2017), "Compressed Sensing using
  Generative Models", on MNIST. A DCGAN generator and a VAE decoder are used as
  priors for recovering images from random Gaussian measurements, and compared
  against a Lasso/DCT sparsity baseline. Course project for Numerical Analysis
  for Machine Learning, MSc Computer Science and Engineering, Politecnico di
  Milano.
keywords:
  - compressed sensing
  - generative models
  - variational autoencoder
  - generative adversarial network
  - inverse problems
license: MIT
